// spec: a typed union's subscript takes one of its own tags (design.md 8.5): an integer or another enum's enumerator is a compile error (until 2026-11-18 it chose the alternative of its number), and a lone name that is both an alternative and a variable in scope is an error naming the qualified spelling
// error: typed_union_subscript_errors.kpp:13: error: the typed union Pin is indexed with a value of type Side: its subscript takes one of its alternatives (`Pin::Tag::Name`, the name alone, or `a` of `alternatives(Pin)`)
// error: typed_union_subscript_errors.kpp:14: error: the typed union Pin is indexed with a value of type int32: its subscript takes one of its alternatives (`Pin::Tag::Name`, the name alone, or `a` of `alternatives(Pin)`)
// error: typed_union_subscript_errors.kpp:16: error: 'Hub' in the subscript of the typed union Pin names its alternative Hub and also a variable in scope: write `Pin::Tag::Hub` for the alternative, or rename the variable
enum Side { Left, Right };
union enum class Pin : u8
{
  { {Position, int}, {Hub, i64} }
};
int main()
{
  Pin pin = Pin::Hub(5);
  pin[Right] = 1;
  pin[0] = 2;
  int Hub = 3;
  return int(pin[Hub]) + Hub;
}
